WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.330
- Our next guest is a
platinum selling artist,

00:00:02.330 --> 00:00:05.350
whose latest album is called
On Earth and in Heaven.

00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:06.790
You can also catch him these days

00:00:06.790 --> 00:00:09.620
on The Masked Singer,
returning March 10th on Fox.

00:00:09.620 --> 00:00:11.998
Everybody say hello to
my friend, Robin Thicke!

00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:14.998
(audience cheering)

00:00:16.625 --> 00:00:18.673
It's so nice to see you.

00:00:18.673 --> 00:00:20.050
- It's so nice to see you.

00:00:20.050 --> 00:00:20.883
How are you?

00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:21.716
- I'm so good.

00:00:21.716 --> 00:00:22.740
Your hair is a little longer.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.800
I saw you turn to the side
during like the commercial.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:26.070
Your hair is like a little longer.

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:26.903
- Yeah.

00:00:26.903 --> 00:00:27.736
- I like it.

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:29.491
- I'm almost full Swayze at this point.

00:00:29.491 --> 00:00:31.970
It's Dirty Dancing Swayze. (chuckles)

00:00:31.970 --> 00:00:33.530
- Well, speaking of Swayze,

00:00:33.530 --> 00:00:35.240
I feel like you're always smooth.

00:00:35.240 --> 00:00:37.840
So like, was there ever
like an awkward phase?

00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:39.490
Please say yes.

00:00:39.490 --> 00:00:40.323
- Oh yes.

00:00:40.323 --> 00:00:44.200
Oh, I've had many, but probably
my most awkward phase was,

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.070
you know, when I was about 13 and 14

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:48.720
and I was into everything hip hop.

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:53.050
I wore my overalls backwards
with crossed colors.

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:56.470
I had different color legs and yeah.

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.560
So, it was me trying to be as hip hop

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:00.360
and Bell Biv DeVoe as possible

00:01:00.360 --> 00:01:02.200
was probably my awkward phase.

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:03.890
- Oh my gosh, Bell Biv DeVoe.

00:01:03.890 --> 00:01:06.100
That's an all skate y'all,
a lot of those songs.

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:08.090
Well, you write from life experience.

00:01:08.090 --> 00:01:09.850
So, what's an unusual moment

00:01:09.850 --> 00:01:11.920
that inspired a song on this album?

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:14.550
- Well, on this album
there was a great moment

00:01:14.550 --> 00:01:17.250
where I was jamming with the
band and we were getting,

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:19.780
we're getting ready to go on tour.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:22.070
And then my beautiful daughter, Lola,

00:01:22.070 --> 00:01:25.140
who at the time was just
about one years old.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:28.220
She came in and we started,

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:31.300
I started singing Lola, Lola, Lola, Lola.

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:35.180
And we ended up with this great
kind of Spanish salsa jam,

00:01:35.180 --> 00:01:40.180
you know, to honor my two
daughters, Lola and Mia.

00:01:40.290 --> 00:01:41.430
- That's so cool.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.540
I love when random
stuff like that happens.

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:44.875
It's funny how life kind of does that.

00:01:44.875 --> 00:01:47.990
- We love in music and in art,

00:01:47.990 --> 00:01:50.910
we love those magical mistakes
that you end up keeping,

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:51.743
you know?

00:01:51.743 --> 00:01:52.900
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:01:52.900 --> 00:01:56.560
So what about, I heard about,
is it the Shooter song?

00:01:56.560 --> 00:01:57.570
What's that one?

00:01:57.570 --> 00:01:58.620
- Yes.

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:01.370
Well, the Shooter song was
actually on my first album.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.040
When I was around 18 years old

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:05.080
there was a crazy story that took place

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.060
where I was in the bank getting some cash

00:02:08.060 --> 00:02:11.430
for a weekend vacation
and the bank got robbed.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:13.320
So, these two guys came in with, you know,

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.090
masks, automatic weapons,

00:02:15.090 --> 00:02:17.370
and told everyone to
get down on the ground.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:19.470
And so I ended up writing this whole song

00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.540
about my experience going
through a live bank robbery.

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:25.890
And then years later,
Little Wayne ended up

00:02:25.890 --> 00:02:28.485
doing a verse on it
and put it on his album

00:02:28.485 --> 00:02:31.863
and he won a Grammy on
that album actually.

00:02:31.863 --> 00:02:33.414
- That's amazing though.

00:02:33.414 --> 00:02:35.280
That's an incredible experience.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.113
Somebody told me that

00:02:36.113 --> 00:02:37.680
and I was like wait what?

00:02:37.680 --> 00:02:38.513
I didn't know that.

00:02:38.513 --> 00:02:40.560
- It was pretty wild
- That's traumatizing.

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.723
- It was a little traumatizing.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:48.840
However, I think once it was
over, I was okay with it.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:50.250
It reminded me of the movies.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.480
It just, it seemed kind
of surreal at the time.

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.040
I didn't really feel threatened
as much as I did like,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:58.393
wow this really does look like a movie.

00:02:59.260 --> 00:03:00.093
- Oh my God.

00:03:00.093 --> 00:03:00.926
You're different than me.

00:03:00.926 --> 00:03:02.890
I'd be in therapy the next morning.

00:03:02.890 --> 00:03:05.080
I'd be like, it was tragic.

00:03:05.080 --> 00:03:05.913
- Well, you know what it was,

00:03:05.913 --> 00:03:08.100
it was probably because
they were very young.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.670
They seemed like they
were 19, 18 year old kids.

00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:13.950
They looked just like my
friends dressed up in masks.

00:03:13.950 --> 00:03:14.800
You know what I mean?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:15.633
I didn't see,

00:03:15.633 --> 00:03:18.810
so I didn't see these
big muscular adult men.

00:03:18.810 --> 00:03:21.480
I saw like two slim teenage men come in

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:22.313
- Making poor decisions.

00:03:22.313 --> 00:03:23.200
- And they looked like my buddies.

00:03:23.200 --> 00:03:25.100
So, there was something
strange about that,

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:26.590
that probably. (chuckles)

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:27.820
- Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:30.480
That probably was, yeah, I
guess that was different,

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:32.330
but you have a new album called

00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:33.856
On Earth and in Heaven
we were talking about it.

00:03:33.856 --> 00:03:36.530
So, what's the inspiration
for this one, man?

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:37.880
- Well, you know, Kelly, the last,

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.600
since I saw you last,
it's been a whirlwind.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.720
You know, I had this
blurred lines success,

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.140
and then I had, I got divorced

00:03:47.140 --> 00:03:49.160
and I, my father passed away.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.810
My beloved father passed away.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:51.947
My house burnt down.

00:03:51.947 --> 00:03:53.790
My manager passed away.

00:03:53.790 --> 00:03:57.210
My mentor passed away
last year when COVID hit.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:03:59.870
So, I've been through so much loss

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:02.240
and it's been a tough road back,

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:04.250
but I've really learned to take all

00:04:04.250 --> 00:04:05.470
that life has thrown at me

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:08.290
and try to turn it into
something beautiful and positive.

00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:10.030
I have three new children,

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:14.210
a total of four now that keep me smiling

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:16.340
and working hard every day.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.050
And so this album is a testament

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:20.160
called On Earth and in Heaven

00:04:20.160 --> 00:04:22.849
of the people that have
passed and moved on

00:04:22.849 --> 00:04:25.520
and the influence that they've had on me

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:28.000
and they still have on me,
even though they're gone.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:29.900
And the other people
that are here on earth

00:04:29.900 --> 00:04:33.240
like my fiance, my
mother, and my four kids

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:35.490
that give me strength and, you know,

00:04:35.490 --> 00:04:37.920
make me want to be the
best person I can be.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:38.753
- Absolutely.

00:04:38.753 --> 00:04:40.760
That's a lot of tragedy.

00:04:40.760 --> 00:04:42.560
That's a lot of major things happening

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:45.385
and I'm surprised it
wasn't a country album.

00:04:45.385 --> 00:04:46.218
Like that was like,

00:04:46.218 --> 00:04:49.455
that was the makings of
a great country album.

00:04:49.455 --> 00:04:51.770
- Yeah, soul music and country music,

00:04:51.770 --> 00:04:54.340
they go hand in hand.
- They're cousins.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.230
I've always said they're
cousins, I believe that.

00:04:56.230 --> 00:04:57.870
Well, you're performing for us later.

00:04:57.870 --> 00:04:59.820
So, what are you gonna be singing?

00:04:59.820 --> 00:05:02.360
- I'll be singing a
song called Lucky Star.

00:05:02.360 --> 00:05:04.540
Which is actually the last
song I wrote for the album.

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.020
And it's dedicated to my father

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:10.120
and Andre Horrell, who was
my mentor for 20 years,

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.810
and executive produced all my albums.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:15.180
And it's about, we all have
a lucky star in our life

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:18.210
that when we're alone, we
know we're not really alone.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:20.880
And we talk to that energy
and we pray to that energy

00:05:20.880 --> 00:05:24.310
and it helps guide us through
the tough times, you know?

00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:26.630
- Oh, that's a beautiful,
beautiful thought.

00:05:26.630 --> 00:05:27.830
I love that.

00:05:27.830 --> 00:05:29.670
Well, everybody Robin's album is called

00:05:29.670 --> 00:05:31.317
On Earth and in Heaven.

